# Timers that installation and convergence may enable automatically.
#
# Single source of truth, read by install.sh and by bin/domum-media's
# sync_timer_overrides. One unit name per line; blank lines and # comments are
# ignored.
#
# RULE: only protective or read-only timers belong here. A timer that deploys,
# stages, or applies application or image changes must NEVER be listed, because
# installation and convergence run unattended and must not be able to start
# deploying on their own. Enabling such a timer is a deliberate operator action.
#
# Deliberately NOT listed:
#
#   domum-media-image-refresh.timer
#       Stages and applies container image updates. Image discovery must not
#       imply deployment, and the update/apply/rollback pipeline has not been
#       audited. See docs/P0-BACKUP-BASELINE.md and CLAUDE.md.
#
#   domum-media-btrfs-scrub.timer
#       Read-only, and protective -- it is the only thing that LOOKS for silent
#       corruption. Still deliberately not auto-enabled: enabling it means a
#       scrub WILL start unattended on the first Sunday of a month, and
#       starting one is an operator decision. Run it once by hand first
#       (`domum-media storage scrub start`) and read what it reports.
#       See docs/BTRFS-SCRUB-PLAN.md.
#
#   domum-media-weekly-report.timer
#       Opt-in reporting, and now the only thing that PROACTIVELY tells the
#       operator anything: it writes the weekly report and then runs
#       `health-notify`, which mails only when something needs attention. Still
#       deliberately not auto-enabled -- it sends mail, so enabling it is an
#       operator decision, and its output should be reviewed on the host once
#       first (`domum-media health-notify --dry-run`).
#       See docs/WEEKLY-REPORT.md.

domum-media-backup.timer
domum-media-check.timer
domum-media-btrfs-snapshot.timer
domum-media-host-update.timer
domum-media-dr-reminder.timer
